WEBVTT

NOTE English track for the videocc PoC. Cue timings match ja.vtt.

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.000
This is a PoC for switching subtitle languages.

2
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:09.000
The video is a test pattern generated with ffmpeg.
The clock in the middle shows the playback position.

3
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:14.000
Use the CC button at the bottom right,
or the language buttons above, to switch subtitles.

4
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:20.000
English subtitles aim for 42 characters per line. This cue is deliberately long to check how wrapping behaves.

5
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:25.000
Drag the zoom slider up to 200% to see
whether the subtitles get clipped with the video.

6
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:30.000
In Safari the browser draws the cues itself,
so they are expected to scale with the video.

7
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:35.000
In Chrome and Firefox, Video.js draws the cues
into a separate element.

8
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:40.000
The surgeon holds the needle driver in the right hand
and stabilizes the tissue with forceps in the left.

9
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:45.000
Enter the tissue perpendicular to the surface
and follow the curve of the needle with a wrist rotation.

10
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:50.000
Secure the knot with three throws.

11
00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:55.000
On iPhone, the playsinline attribute changes
how fullscreen behaves.

12
00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:59.500
That is the end of the PoC subtitles.
